id: pm-context-9xfx
title: Preserve append-only provenance history during review repair
description: "A review correction must retain every original provenance-bearing history event and append an explicit, replayable record of the normalization instead of rewriting prior audit history."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-28T19:55:04.883Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:34:03.228Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T19:59:49.593Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T19:59:49.593Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
resolution: Fixed scanner regressions and recorded provenance normalization append-only.
expected_result: "Every reachable publish is audited, and provenance history corrections preserve the original event records and chain."
actual_result: The focused regression suite and release gate pass; history chain drift is zero and correction events enumerate all legacy role removals.
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T19:55:22.103Z",pi-agent,"Decision: fixed the five scanner/verifier findings with regression tests. The seven history streams were restored byte-for-byte to their prior events and each received a non-empty history_repair context listing every removed role observation by event index; the old event provenance remains preserved for replay and audit. Health still reports the legacy domain warning by design, while history drift and chain validation pass."
  "2026-08-28T20:08:56.494Z",pi-agent,"Follow-up finding fixed after the next Greptile round: negated npm Boolean options such as no-fund are now recognized generically, so their following publish token is not consumed as an option value. The regression fixture fails when this rule is removed."
  "2026-08-28T20:25:49.240Z",pi-agent,"Second review follow-up fixed: the complete npm Boolean option set is now represented, and unknown negated options are handled as Boolean flags. The positive fund form was reproduced, covered by a regression test, and no longer hides publish."
  "2026-08-28T20:34:03.227Z",pi-agent,"Third review follow-up fixed: foreground-scripts and strict-npmrc were missing from the Boolean option inventory; both are now included. The Boolean inventory was cross-checked against the installed npm definition table, and the foreground-scripts regression remains visible to the audit."
files[10]{path,scope,note}:
